# Written for this pack by BurN-30 (GPL-3.0). Replaces 04-salle-des-thanes.guide (adapted from Aurum's
# chapter aurum-druid/hall-of-thanes, Aurums Night Elf Druid Guide 0.4.37, GPL-3.0) on Polestar's own
# route. Sources: Polestar 0.4.2.2 (GPL-3.0), its `when dungeon "The Hall of Thanes"` steps of
# forever/alliance/02-westfall (Thom Filch and Afadra Dunwall west of the High Seat, the door at
# Ironforge 28.2,47.7 from players' recordings, the tram from Stormwind), data/dungeon-runs.json and
# its Dungeons codex (quests, rewards, the four bosses); quest data of Polestar's forever-db; the way
# down, the heirlooms and the bosses from Warcraft Tavern's Hall of Thanes guides (read 23/11/2026),
# rewritten. Not played in game yet.
#
# Self-contained chapter for Polestar's route: the Groupe Alliance module offers it once The People's
# Militia (13) is handed in to Gryan Stoutmantle, the last Sentinel Hill stop of
# forever/alliance/02-westfall (about level 16, every race), whose next stop is Stormwind: the
# chapter rides the tram to Ironforge from there and the route's Stormwind steps follow its end.
# Since 0.13.0 the chapter has the id its guide had up to 0.12.x (groupe-alliance/04-salle-des-thanes): a tab saved on it opens
# the chapter.
#
# Compared with Polestar's run: the same Ironforge quests and the same door; added An Ancient Grudge
# (96395, given and taken back inside), Ironforge's flight path, the bosses one by one, and Old
# Ironforge Incursion (96393) for whoever can take it. Earthseer Farsen's chain (96408 to 96391) is
# done by the Dwarf and Gnome starts; Farsen offers 96393 only after Underground Map (96391), from a
# Dark Iron Map that drops: an optional trip to his camp, shown only when the quest is available.
# The old chapter's trip to Steelgrill's Depot for every race (about 20 minutes) is left out, as is
# Knowledge in the Deeps (971, Blackfathom Deeps, level 23).
guide groupe-alliance/04-salle-des-thanes
title Dungeon · The Hall of Thanes (14-19)
folder Group Alliance
category Dungeons
faction Alliance
levels 14-19
zone Ironforge

step Stormwind: the tram to Ironforge
  zone Stormwind City
  tip The Hall of Thanes: a 5-player Forever dungeon under Ironforge, levels 13 to 20 in the group finder: at 15 or more it goes well. Its quests are taken in Ironforge, a few steps from its door, and handed in there.
  note Keep 5 free quest log slots. Everyone takes the quests on their own; meet at the door, west of the High Seat.
  fly "Stormwind"
  goto 64.5,7.5 "Tram to Ironforge"

step Ironforge: Thom Filch and Afadra Dunwall
  zone Ironforge
  tip Gryth Thurden, the gryphon master, stands in the Great Forge: take the flight path on the way. Then west past the High Seat: Thom Filch and Afadra Dunwall stand a few steps apart, by the way down to the dungeon.
  getfp "Ironforge"
  accept 96403                                -- Thom Filch: Important Heirlooms
  accept 96394                                -- Afadra Dunwall: The Restless Dead

step Earthseer Farsen: Old Ironforge Incursion (optional)
  when available 96393
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Only for whoever handed in Underground Map (the Dark Iron Map of the spies, in the Dwarf and Gnome starts): Earthseer Farsen gives Old Ironforge Incursion, the head of the last boss for King Magni, about 3,200 XP. Out of Ironforge's gate, east past Kharanos to his camp above Gol'Bolar Quarry: about 10 minutes there and back. Short on time? Skip it.
  accept 96393 @64.8,58.4                     -- Earthseer Farsen

step Before entering the Hall of Thanes
  zone Ironforge
  tip From the High Seat, the cobwebbed passage on the left goes down to the door. Mind the edges on the way: the lava below kills.
  note In the log: Important Heirlooms (Thom Filch) and The Restless Dead (Afadra Dunwall); Old Ironforge Incursion for whoever took it from Earthseer Farsen. Share each quest with the group: click it in the quest log, then Share.
  goto 28.2,47.7 "The Hall of Thanes" r 20

step The Hall of Thanes: along the way
  along until hot-durgen
  tip The ghosts of the first chambers are Afadra's: Enraged Apparitions and Tormented Souls. The Dwarven Heirlooms lie all over the dungeon, many on candle-lit ledges of the corridors; the vaults of the last room hold enough for everyone, so nobody needs to race for them.
  complete 96394                              -- The Restless Dead: the ghosts of the first chambers
  collect 274289 x8 quest 96403               -- Dwarven Heirloom

step Anvilmar's Rest: Faldrim Anvilmar
  tip The Ghostly Attendant waits in the chamber west of the entrance: her quest is the first boss. Faldrim walks round the great tomb of the next room: clear the ghosts around it first. His Anvilmar's Curse slows the tank's attacks and spells for a long time: a Mage or a Druid can remove it. His Mind Blast can be interrupted.
  accept 96395                                -- Ghostly Attendant: An Ancient Grudge
  kill 261306 quest 96395                     -- Faldrim Anvilmar
  turnin 96395                                -- Ghostly Attendant, on the way back too

step The fire elemental of the cavern
  tip South-east out of Anvilmar's Rest: Dark Iron dwarves from here on. Bloodhound Runts leave a disease that makes their target take more damage (Stoneform or a poultice clears it); Engineers throw dynamite; Summoners call fire elementals: interrupt them. Ranged players can shoot the kegs of blasting powder to hit the packs around them. In the natural cavern, the fire elemental boss burns everyone near him: kill the Dark Iron Summoner beside him first, ranged players keep away, and the healer watches the melee too.
  note Its name differs between sources (Infurnus in the dungeon journal, Magmatus in the guides): the only fire elemental boss of the dungeon.

step Plunder
  tip Back in the halls, a pack of four Dark Iron dwarves stands between two kegs: shoot the kegs from afar first. Plunder, a stone golem, walks the hallway after it: pull him away from the others and tank him with his back to a wall, as he knocks back and charges whoever stands close.
  kill 261311                                 -- Plunder

step The Reliquary of Kings: Durgen Dirgehammer
  label hot-durgen
  tip North over the bridge of the Lesser Stone Golems to the round last room. Clear it before the pull: Durgen fears the whole group and whatever is left joins in. Kill his two Lesser Stone Golems first. Each player on Old Ironforge Incursion loots the head. Behind one of the vault doors of the room, the Treaty of Understanding: each player clicks it for their own quest.
  kill 261319                                 -- Durgen Dirgehammer
  collect 274286 quest 96393 optional         -- Durgen Dirgehammer's Head
  accept 98423 item 281030                    -- Treaty of Understanding, behind a vault door of the room

step King Magni: Old Ironforge Incursion
  when onquest 96393
  zone Ironforge
  tip Back out the way you came in: King Magni sits on the High Seat, east of the door.
  turnin 96393 optional                       -- King Magni Bronzebeard

step Ironforge rewards
  zone Ironforge
  tip Back out the way you came in. King Magni sits on the High Seat, east of the door. Last stop of the chapter: the route's own guide comes back once these are handed in, and goes on in Stormwind (the tram from Tinker Town).
  turnin 96403                                -- Thom Filch
  turnin 96394                                -- Afadra Dunwall
  turnin 98423                                -- King Magni Bronzebeard
